Z||000002||hugh||10-17-2000||09:07 PM||||My v8 GT goes   rump rump rump<BR>But seriously,what do you need to record and send sound?||||reg||5
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||10-17-2000||09:21 PM||||the easiest way is with a laptop and a microphone, but you can also use a hand held tape recorder and get a double ended 3.5mm audio cable, put one end in the speaker jack of the recorder, and the other end into the line in on your computer, then record it that way. the way I capture most of my sounds is with a stationary video camera (my brother holding it) while i drive by, then i record the video (and sound) onto my computer with my capture card. if people have video cameras, i can always send a blank tape for you to record on. this method works very well, because fiero videos are even cooler than fiero sounds!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1012904&a=7460599&p=25516673"> ||||reg||1
